Defines the list of components, raw materials, quantities, and operations required to manufacture a finished product or sub-assembly.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Single-level and multi-level BOMs
Production planning and material requirement planning (MRP)
Cost calculation of finished goods
Engineering changes and version control
Phantom / modular BOMs (kit assembly)
By-products and co-products management
Used by Manufacturing Orders, Work Orders, and MRP scheduler

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread)
Key Fields:
product_tmpl_id / product_id (the finished product)
code (reference), type (normal / phantom / kits)
version (for engineering BOM versioning)
bom_line_ids → One2many to mrp.bom.line (components)
operation_ids → One2many to mrp.routing.workcenter (operations)
ready_to_produce (selection), consumption (flexible / strict)
company_id, active

Critical Hooks: onchange_product_id, _compute_total_cost, action_compute_bom_cost, explosion logic (_bom_explode)
Security: mrp.group_mrp_manager + company rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
bill of materials, BOM, BOM structure, manufacturing BOM, product recipe, component list, multi-level BOM, phantom BOM, kit BOM, production BOM, engineering BOM, mrp.bom, BOM line, routing
Related Models (most joined):

mrp.bom.line (child components)
product.product / product.template
mrp.routing.workcenter / mrp.workcenter
mrp.production (manufacturing order)
mrp.workorder
stock.warehouse

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
mrp.bom is Odoo’s core Bill of Materials model that defines how a product is manufactured with product_tmpl_id, type (normal/phantom), version, bom_line_ids (components with qty), and operation_ids. It powers BOM explosion, material requirements planning, production costing, multi-level structures, and is the foundation of the entire Manufacturing (MRP) module, tightly integrated with inventory, work orders, and production orders.